From: Andrew Udvare <audvare@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] go.mod: bump modules that break on Go 1.27

golang.org/x/tools: gqlgen loads packages through x/tools/go/packages. Go
1.27 writes export data version 5, which x/tools before v0.50.0 cannot
decode. gqlgen discards its log output by default, so `go generate` exits 1
with no message.

github.com/enetx/http: enetx/http2 has a go1.27-tagged file that reads
Server.DisableClientPriority, which the enetx/http fork only gained in
v1.0.29.

Generated with
`go mod edit -require=golang.org/x/tools@v0.50.0 -require=github.com/enetx/http@v1.0.29`
followed by `go mod tidy`.
---
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 module github.com/stashapp/stash
 
-go 1.25.0
+go 1.26.0
 
 require (
 	github.com/99designs/gqlgen v0.17.73
@@ -58,12 +58,12 @@
